{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ne={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n \\\"test_names\\\":[\\\"TestAssuranceRemovedVoterCannotConfirmReadIndex\\\"],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"membership-handle-config-change\\\",\\\"raft-remove-node\\\",\\\"peer-response-filter\\\",\\\"lw-remote-lookup\\\",\\\"leader-readindex-admission\\\",\\\"readindex-confirm\\\",\\\"leader-heartbeat-resp\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"raft-remove-node\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"removeNode\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1196,\\\"end_line\\\":1213},\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"peer-response-filter\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Peer.Handle\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":185,\\\"end_line\\\":196},\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"leader-readindex-admission\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handleLeaderReadIndex\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1662,\\\"end_line\\\":1695},\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"readindex-confirm\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"readIndex.confirm\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":77,\\\"end_line\\\":116}],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Confirmation after a live removal. Voters 1 and 2 apply a RemoveNode config change for node 3, a ReadIndex request from node 2 is queued at the leader, and the confirming heartbeat response is delivered first from removed node 3 and then from current voter 2.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Three real in-process Raft Peer handlers bootstrap membership {1,2,3} and node 1 is leader with a committed current-term no-op; each node uses a test-only in-memory ILogDB.\\\",\n   \\\"The removal is applied through Peer.ApplyConfigChange on the two remaining voters, which is the call the surrounding node makes when it applies a committed RemoveNode entry.\\\",\n   \\\"The confirming responses carry the queued context and arrive with a zero term, as heartbeat responses do; they are delivered through the real Peer admission path used for network messages.\\\",\n   \\\"Production code is unchanged.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\n   \\\"Node 3 does not run the removal itself; only the remaining voters' maps are updated, which is the leader-side state that decides admissions.\\\",\n   \\\"No transport, persistence or restart path is exercised.\\\",\n   \\\"The direct-to-raft admission layer is covered by a separate receipt for an unknown sender; this case exercises the Peer layer only.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness launches three real Raft peers with bootstrap membership {1,2,3} and ticks node 1 until its current-term no-op is committed. Both remaining voters then apply a RemoveNode config change for node 3 and pump their updates, and the run records that the voter set is now {1,2}. Node 2 forwards a ReadIndex request carrying context {303,3003} to the leader. A HeartbeatResp carrying that context from node 3 is delivered to the leader and the run records how many ReadIndex replies addressed to node 2 it produced; the same response is then delivered from voter 2 and the reply count is recorded again.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"After a node is removed from the voter set, a delayed heartbeat response from that node must not satisfy the ReadIndex quorum, while a response from a current voter must confirm the request.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The applied RemoveNode path deletes the node from the raft role maps, Peer.Handle admits response messages only from senders in those maps, and readIndex.confirm confirms only when enough admitted responses arrive. The experiment exercises those real paths and changes only which node answers.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"read_queued\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"readindex_queued\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"request_id\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"node2-read-R\\\",\\\"reference\\\":None}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"removed_voter_response\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"request_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"read_queued\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replies_to_2\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0,\\\"reference\\\":None},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":None,\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"sender\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3,\\\"reference\\\":None}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A response from the removed node must not confirm the queued read.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"current_voter_response\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"request_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"read_queued\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replies_to_2\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1,\\\"reference\\\":None},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":None,\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"sender\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2,\\\"reference\\\":None}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A response from a current voter must confirm the queued read and produce a reply.\\\"}]}\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Extend the admission receipt to the live transition that the former-voter question actually describes. The remaining voters apply a real RemoveNode for node 3, a read is queued at the leader, and the confirming heartbeat response is delivered first from the removed node and then from a current voter. \\\"\n \\\"Local construction runs showed zero replies after the removed node's response and one reply after the voter's response, so a delayed response from a removed voter does not satisfy the quorum under the applied transition.\\\"),\n \\\"experiment\\\":e}, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -12\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
